Section 2(v) of the Act reads as under:
2. (v) food' means any article used as food or drink for human consumption other than drugs and water and includes-- (a) any article which ordinarily enters into, or is used in the composition or preparation of, human food;
(b) any flavouring matter or condiments; and (c) any other article which the Central Government may, having regard to its use,
nature, substance or quality, declare, by notification in the Official Gazette, as food for the purposes of this Act;
